cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GSSK — General Systems Simulation Kernel"
message: "If you use this software or the conformance whitepaper, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maud
    given-names: Sholto
abstract: "GSSK is a C99 numerical kernel for simulating systems expressed in Howard T. Odum's Energy Systems Language. A model is a JSON description of storages, sources, sinks and the pathways between them; the kernel integrates the resulting system of ordinary differential equations using Euler, RK4 or adaptive Dormand–Prince methods, and tracks several carriers — energy, material, money, information — independently over the same network. Odum's symbol vocabulary is implemented as node primitives and composite archetypes, with emergy and transformity accounting over the same topology, and deterministic snapshot and replay for reproducible runs. Bindings are provided for C, Python, JavaScript/WebAssembly and Swift."
keywords:
  - systems ecology
  - energy systems language
  - Howard T. Odum
  - emergy
  - transformity
  - general systems theory
  - system dynamics
  - ordinary differential equations
  - numerical simulation
  - C99
  - WebAssembly
